ARTICLEIV-MEMBERSHIP
Section1.Eligibility.An individual shall become an on-voting member of the Corporation upon purchase of a
other privileges as The Board Directors may determine from time to time.The voting members of the
Corporations hall be those persons, over18yearsofage, defined as the Governing Body in Article V, Section1
of these bylaws.The Boardof Directors will set theprice of a season membership andunder no circumstances
will the price be less than$25peryear.
Section 2.Fees.Thepurchase price of the season membership shall be determined bythe Board of Directors
and shall cover the fiscal year as defined in Article V ll of thesebylaws.
Section3.Honorary Life Membership.The Board of Directors may, atits discretion, grant an Honorary Life
Membership to individuals who have contributed significantly to the promotion of the Corporation.
Section4.Temporary Member.A Temporary Member is anyone who buys a ticket to anyone performance or
who is given a ticket to a performance that is purchased by someone else.
ARTICLEV-GOVERNING BODY
President for Administration/Secretary: D)Vice President for Programming; E)Vice President for the Fund
Development, andF)additional board members.Allmembers of the Board of Directors must be season
members each year.
Section 2.Standing Committees.There shall be four Standing Committees: A)Finance, B)administration, C)
as Chairand Cheyenne Little Theatre Players Board Members, which shall be equitably assigned among the
Standing Committees by the Board President(after receiving input from each committee chair and board
the Committee Chair with input from the member of the committee.
