```text
Section 6.Vacancies.All vacancies occurring during the year will be filled through election by the Board of
one of the Vice President s to finish the term.Anytime served as President for more than sixmonthsis
considered afullterm.Election will be for the term remaining in the office to be filled.The Board of
Directors, by a majority vote, may declare any position vacant or remove any member for reasons of absence
or any other just cause.
ARTICLEVI-POWERS AND DUTIES
Section1.The Boardof Directors has the powerto: A)establish and enforce policies and guidelines for the
Corporation; B)review corporate and fiscal performance for the Corporation; C)create ordissolve any
portion of the Corporation with a two-thirds (2/3) vote of the fullboard; D) initiate and approve bylaws; E)
approve selection of playsand directors, dates of plays, and special projects ofthe Corporation; and F)hirea
Managing Director and supervise his or her performance.
Section2.The President has the responsibility to: A)call and reside overall meetings of the Board of Directors
and the Executive Committee; B)beanex-officio member of all committees except the nominating sub-
committee; C)act as liaison person betweenthe Board of Directors and the professional staff; D)be the
and other such necessary instruments on behalf of the Corporation; and G)ensure that all new Board of
bylaws and committee responsibilities.Inthe eventof the President's absence or inability to serve, thefour
Vice President s shall determine the proper temporary leadership.
Section3.The Executive Committee has the responsibility to: A)recommend, monitor, and evaluate the goals,
Directors with recommendations; andC)act with the full authority of the Board of Directors in times of
emergency when the Board of Directors are unable to meet or a quorum to transact business cannot be
obtained.
Section4.The Vice President for Finance/Treasurer has the responsibility to: A)Fulfill all responsibilities of the
Presidents in the absence thereof; B)serve on the Executive Committee; C)chair the Finance Committee, the
